            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nI don't have the means to reproduce this, so I'd have to ask for your help to find the best fix.\r\nCould you, please, try replacing both instances of `vim.fn.filereadable(path) == 1` ([this](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/0a8a1072137d916406507c941698a4bfa9dbbe7a/lua/mini/bracketed.lua#L1732) and [this](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/0a8a1072137d916406507c941698a4bfa9dbbe7a/lua/mini/bracketed.lua#L1751)) with `vim.loop.fs_stat(path) ~= nil` and see if it fixes the hanging issue?\r\n\r\n------\r\n\r\nAs a side note, I'd also suggest creating an issue in vim/vim repo about this behavior of `filereadable()`. I don't think it should ever hang.",
