        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "After some investigation, I think that removing that check is safe without even an option. As far as I understand/remember, it was there mostly for memory reasons (to not track entries from 'oldfiles' which are not already present on disk or were not there to begin with). This should help with indefinite hanging on `require('mini.bracketed').setup()`, but using `oldfile` target would still be affected, as it uses `vim.fn.filereadable()` for normalization.\n\nI tried to reproduce locally (by mounting flash drive and removing it without first unmounting it), but could not reproduce. If indefinite hanging on `vim.fn.filereadable()` in described use case is still reproducible, please consider opening issue in 'vim/vim' repo (not even Neovim, as that part of code base is from Vim).",
